unctionally with sales, operations, and product teams to drive data-informed decisions. Optimize processes and workflows using marketing technology (MarTech) tools like Segment CDP and Twilio Engage. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business, Statistics, or a related field (Master's preferred). 5+ years of experience in marketing analytics, revenue marketing, or a related field. Proficiency in SQL, Excel, and Power BI. Experience with Alteryx or similar data automation tools. Strong understanding of B2B marketing and revenue alignment frameworks. Familiarity with Oracle Eloqua, Segment, Twilio Engage, and Snowflake. Excellent communication skills with the ability to present complex data clearly to stakeholders. Soft Skills: Strategic Thinking – You see the big picture and connect data to business outcomes. Cross-Functional Collaboration – You work seamlessly with teams across the organization. Stakeholder Engagement – You influence decisions at all levels with data-backed insights. Process Optimization – You streamline workflows for efficiency and scalability. Adaptability – You thrive in fast-paced, evolving environments. Attention to Detail – You ensure accuracy in every analysis and report. Project Management – You juggle multiple priorities and deliver on time. Disclaimer: Please note that, due to the current integration framework, this opportunity is currently available exclusively to employees of Altair and DISW. While there is a possibility that the position may be made available to all Siemens employees through a future external posting, this is not guaranteed. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation during this transitional period. This communication does not constitute a promise or guarantee of future employment opportunities beyond the current scope. Why us? Working at Siemens Software means flexibility - Choosing between working at home and the office at other times is the norm here. We offer great benefits and rewards, as you'd e